SS 03", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.rssFeedRead", "onError": "continueRegularOutput", "position": [1600, 620], "parameters": {"url": "https://the-decoder.com/feed/", "options": {}}, "typeVersion": 1.1, "alwaysOutputData": true}, {"id": "31da3f86-a150-4cd4-83bd-57bcb348f7c3", "name": "My RSS 04", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.rssFeedRead", "onError": "continueRegularOutput", "position": [1600, 840], "parameters": {"url": "https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml", "options": {"ignoreSSL": false}}, "typeVersion": 1.1, "alwaysOutputData": true}, {"id": "a2e2bf11-d56a-470f-b183-751ff5a2d7f9", "name": "Sticky Note1", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1540, 1000], "parameters": {"content": "## About RSS\nYou can add how many RSS you want"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "90ea767f-aa1f-4475-8378-85f9b34487eb", "name": "Send resum to  Whatsapp", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [3160, 500], "parameters": {"url": "yoururlapi.com", "method": "POST", "options": {}, "sendBody": true, "authentication": "genericCredentialType", "bodyParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "phone", "value": "=your phone number"}, {"name": "message", "value": "={{ $json.output }}"}]}, "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"}, "credentials": {"httpHeaderAuth": {"id": "GZs4cdCRPLFqDfDX", "name": "Automata OS API"}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "55a91be7-2fe8-45ea-9ac5-51e90a9bb2c9", "name": "Sticky Note2", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [3100, 700], "parameters": {"content": "## About Resum\nyou can send to your whatsapp api, or email, drive..."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "16acc038-b6f3-4a7d-a2d9-415c4287532b", "name": "Sticky Note3", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1200, 680], "parameters": {"content": "## About Trgger\nSet trigger how you wish"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "47783f2d-e603-4325-9031-09d3eefe9fcd", "name": "Sticky Note4", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [2820, 700], "parameters": {"content": "## System message (change if you want)\nI've received 10 news articles via RSS. Please analyze them and provide a concise summary of the top 3 to 5 main highlights. My goal is to get a quick overview of what's most relevant in these articles."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "webhook-automata-injected-1791111459541", "name": "Automata Webhook", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook", "position": [0, 0], "webhookId": "xD6cGHJBF0QwUUc5", "parameters": {"path": "xD6cGHJBF0QwUUc5", "options": {}, "httpMethod": "POST", "responseCode": 200, "responseMode": "onReceived"}, "typeVersion": 1.1}]
r3K6AOqHSQD6ceXL|[{"id": "57fab85a-2f3f-454d-b805-29847b2ea94c", "name": "Schedule Trigger", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger", "position": [784, 624], "parameters": {"rule": {"interval": [{"field": "hours", "hoursInterval": 24}]}}, "typeVersion": 1.2}, {"id": "157eddca-8eb2-41d5-b5bc-81453653c2eb", "name": "Pick the Daily Topic", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [1232, 624], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const now = new Date();\n\nconst trendFeeds = [\n  { category: \"Disconnection & Loss of Meaning\", feed_url: \"https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=loneliness+disconnection+community+crisis&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en\", focus: \"Yoga Sutras\", topic: \"Yoga Sutras: The Thread of Wisdom\" },\n  { category: \"Workplace Stress & Corporate Burnout\", feed_url: \"https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=workplace+stress+burnout+corporate&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en\", focus: \"Pranayama & Nervous System Reset\", topic: \"Pranayama: The Breath of Life\" },\n  { category: \"Sedentary Lifestyle & Physical Tension\", feed_url: \"https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=sedentary+lifestyle+health+posture+pain&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en\", focus: \"Hatha Yoga & Somatic Alignment\", topic: \"Hatha Yoga: Body as Wisdom\" },\n  { category: \"Mental Health & Overwhelm\", feed_url: \"https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=mental+health+anxiety+overwhelm+presence&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en\", focus: \"Spiritual Philosophy & Mindfulness\", topic: \"Spiritual Philosophy: Awakening to the Present\" },\n];\n\n// Rotates on successful publishes, not on the calendar -- re-running the\n// workflow (tests, retries) no longer repeats the same topic. The counter\n// only advances in a separate node placed right after a successful publish.\nconst staticData = $getWorkflowStaticData('global');\nconst idx = (staticData.topicIndex || 0) % trendFeeds.length;\nconst picked = trendFeeds[idx];\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    date: now.toISOString().slice(0, 10),\n    category: picked.category,\n    feed_url: picked.feed_url,\n    focus: picked.focus,\n    topic: picked.topic,\n  },\n}];"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "9fc04b99-a13a-4be3-89ee-617c30bc470a", "name": "Fetch News Headlines", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.rssFeedRead", "position": [1456, 624], "parameters": {"url": "={{ $json.feed_url }}", "options": {}}, "typeVersion": 1.1}, {"id": "55b57245-9d22-40d9-b1f6-2687da52f259", "name": "Build News Context", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [1680, 624], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const items = $input.all();\nconst topArticles = items.slice(0, 3).map(item => ({\n  title: item.json.title,\n  snippet: item.json.contentSnippet || item.json.content || ''\n}));\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    news_context: topArticles,\n    category: $('Pick the Daily Topic').item.json.category,\n    focus: $('Pick the Daily Topic').item.json.focus,\n    topic: $('Pick the Daily Topic').item.json.topic\n  }\n}];"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "bd1ecbc5-00fe-4689-bc6b-2ce881583d5a", "name": "Write the Post with Claude", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent", "maxTries": 3, "position": [1904, 624], "parameters": {"text": "=TODAY'S REAL HEADLINES (Google News):\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.news_context, null, 2) }}\nLENS: {{ $json.category }}\nTRADITION: {{ $json.focus }}\nSERIES: {{ $json.topic }}\n\nPick the single strongest headline above - the one with the most concrete, human detail - and build one Instagram post from it. Produce these fields:\n\nnews_hook - one sentence, max 25 words, factually naming the specific development from the headline you picked: the who/what/where, or the finding, or the number. Everything else refers back to this.\n\nproblem - what that development reveals about how people are actually suffering right now. Concrete and human, not abstract.\n\nsolution - what {{ $json.focus }} teaches about this. Grounded in the real tradition; name the concept or text where there is one.\n\npractice - ONE specific technique with concrete counts or durations, doable in under five minutes, seated, anywhere, with no props. Choose whichever technique family genuinely fits {{ $json.focus }} and today's problem best - do not default to breath-counting unless it is truly the best fit. Vary the family post to post rather than repeating the same pattern:\n  - Breath: a counted inhale/exhale/hold pattern\n  - Body-based: a counted body scan or point-by-point tension release\n  - Sensory grounding: a counted noticing exercise (e.g. naming a fixed number of things per sense)\n  - Repetition: a counted mantra, phrase, or silent repetition practice\n  - Micro-movement: a counted small physical gesture or seated stretch sequence\n  State it in full with its numbers, e.g. \"trace each fingertip slowly, five breaths per hand\" or \"silently repeat the phrase on each exhale, ten times\" - not just \"breathe deeply.\"\n\npost_type - {{ ({ SINGLE_IMAGE: 'always \"SINGLE_IMAGE\".', CAROUSEL: 'always \"CAROUSEL\".' })[$('Your Settings').first().json.post_type_mode] || '\"SINGLE_IMAGE\" when the practice is a single shift or a single breath that fits on one frame. \"CAROUSEL\" when it genuinely needs sequential steps.' }}\n\ncaption - 130 to 200 words BEFORE hashtags, flowing paragraphs, no numbered lists, in this order:\n1. OPEN WITH THE NEWS. Two or three sentences describing the specific development from news_hook: what happened, where, and the number or finding that makes it real. A reader who never saw the headline must understand the story from your caption alone.\n2. ACKNOWLEDGE. One or two sentences naming honestly what that actually feels like for the people living it. No silver lining yet.\n3. BRIDGE. Two or three sentences on what {{ $json.focus }} offers here and why - state the mechanism plainly. No mystical hand-waving.\n4. THE PRACTICE. Two or three sentences giving the technique from `practice` in full, with its counts, so it can be done straight from the caption.\n5. CLOSE. One warm, low-pressure sentence. No \"DM me\", no follow-bait, no growth-hack CTA.\nDo not put hashtags anywhere inside the caption text.\n\nhashtags - 8 to 12 entries, each starting with \"#\". Mix broad tags with ones specific to today's angle.\n\nslides - {{ ({ SINGLE_IMAGE: 'exactly 1 item.', CAROUSEL: 'exactly 4 items.' })[$('Your Settings').first().json.post_type_mode] || 'exactly 1 item for SINGLE_IMAGE, 3 to 5 items for CAROUSEL.' }} Each item:\n  headline - the big line drawn ON the image. HARD LIMIT 6 words and 38 characters. Concrete and specific to this post, never a generic mood phrase. Title Case. No quotation marks, no emoji, no trailing punctuation. Slide 1 names the tension and the final slide names the takeaway.\n  sub - the supporting line drawn ON the image, directly under the headline. HARD LIMIT 12 words and 70 characters. It must carry information the headline does not already have: the count, the mechanism, the step number, the duration. Sentence case. No emoji.\n  body - one or two sentences of editorial context for this slide. This is NOT drawn on the image.\n  visual_prompt - SUBJECT MATTER ONLY, max 30 words: the people, posture, objects, arrows and diagram labels needed. NEVER mention colour, palette, art style, typeface, background or \"flat vector\" - the brand system fixes all of that.", "options": {"systemMessage": "=You are the editorial voice of an Instagram account that connects live world events to Yoga, Pranayama and Spiritual Philosophy.\n\nNON-NEGOTIABLE EDITORIAL RULES\n- GROUNDED. No hype, no mysticism-as-decoration, no overclaiming. Stay inside what the tradition actually says and what a reader can verify in their own body within minutes. Never promise cures, healing or outcomes. Never make medical claims.\n- EMPATHETIC. The news hook is usually distressing. Name the difficulty honestly before you offer anything. Never bypass it with forced positivity.\n- ACTIONABLE. Every post resolves into one specific thing the reader can do, drawn from across the full range of the tradition - breath, posture, movement, sensory grounding, or reframe - with counts or durations. Rotate which of these you reach for; do not let breathwork dominate by default just because it is the most familiar.\n- The news is a DOORWAY, not the subject. State what happened factually and neutrally. Never take a side, never assign blame, never comment on politics or personalities.\n\nTHE SPECIFICITY RULE - this is the one you are most likely to break\nYou are handed real headlines. Your caption must let a reader tell exactly WHICH story this post is answering. Name the concrete development: the who, the what, the where, the sector, the finding, the number. These phrases are FORBIDDEN: \"recent discussions\", \"current events\", \"the news lately\", \"what's happening in the world\", \"conversations around\", \"a lot of people are talking about\". Apply this test before you answer: if your caption would still read fine with a completely different news story pasted in, it has failed and you must rewrite it with the actual specifics.\n\nOn-image copy is display type, not prose. It must be short enough to read on a phone thumbnail, and every character limit given below is a hard limit, not a target."}, "promptType": "define", "hasOutputParser": true}, "retryOnFail": true, "typeVersion": 1.7, "waitBetweenTries": 2000}, {"id": "1fedee77-3050-4eb6-8ef1-9a1470287b02", "name": "Post Output Parser", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured", "position": [2080, 848], "parameters": {"schemaType": "manual", "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"news_hook\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"One sentence, max 25 words, naming the specific development from the chosen headline: who/what/where, or the finding, or the number.\"\n    },\n    \"problem\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"What that development reveals about how people are suffering right now. Concrete and human.\"\n    },\n    \"solution\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"What the tradition teaches about this, grounded in the real tradition. Name the concept or text where there is one.\"\n    },\n    \"practice\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"One specific technique with counts or durations, doable in under five minutes, seated, with no props.\"\n    },\n    \"post_type\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"SINGLE_IMAGE\", \"CAROUSEL\"],\n      \"description\": \"SINGLE_IMAGE for one shift or one breath that fits on a single frame; CAROUSEL when sequential steps are genuinely needed.\"\n    },\n    \"caption\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"130-200 words before hashtags, flowing paragraphs. Order: news specifics, honest acknowledgement, bridge to the tradition with its mechanism, the full practice with counts, warm close. No hashtags inside this text. Must name the actual news story concretely.\"\n    },\n    \"hashtags\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"description\": \"8 to 12 hashtags, each starting with '#'. Mix broad tags with ones specific to today's angle.\"\n    },\n    \"slides\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"headline\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Big line drawn ON the image. Hard limit 6 words and 38 characters. Title Case, concrete, no quotes, no emoji, no trailing punctuation.\"\n          },\n          \"sub\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Supporting line drawn ON the image under the headline. Hard limit 12 words and 70 characters. Must add information the headline lacks: count, mechanism, step number or duration. Sentence case, no emoji.\"\n          },\n          \"body\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"One or two sentences of editorial context. NOT drawn on the image.\"\n          },\n          \"visual_prompt\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Subject matter only, max 30 words: people, posture, objects, arrows, diagram labels. Never mention colour, palette, art style, typeface or background.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"headline\", \"sub\", \"body\", \"visual_prompt\"]\n      },\n      \"description\": \"Exactly 1 item for SINGLE_IMAGE, 3 to 5 items for CAROUSEL.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"news_hook\",\n    \"problem\",\n    \"solution\",\n    \"practice\",\n    \"post_type\",\n    \"caption\",\n    \"hashtags\",\n    \"slides\"\n  ]\n}"}, "typeVersion": 1.2}, {"id": "3ccfce81-a281-4016-850b-45488889bae8", "name": "Normalize & Plan Slides", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [2256, 624], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const o = $json.output || $json;\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Post format. Set post_type_mode on the \"Your Settings\" node:\n//   'AUTO'         -- the AI picks single image or carousel per post\n//   'SINGLE_IMAGE' -- always one image\n//   'CAROUSEL'     -- always a carousel\n// The prompt is told the same thing, but a prompt is not a constraint, so the\n// rule is enforced here as well.\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nconst settings = $('Your Settings').first().json;\nconst nSlides = (o.slides || []).length;\nif (settings.post_type_mode === 'SINGLE_IMAGE' || settings.post_type_mode === 'CAROUSEL') {\n  o.post_type = settings.post_type_mode;\n}\nif (o.post_type !== 'SINGLE_IMAGE' && o.post_type !== 'CAROUSEL') {\n  o.post_type = nSlides > 1 ? 'CAROUSEL' : 'SINGLE_IMAGE';\n}\nif (o.post_type === 'CAROUSEL' && nSlides < 2) {\n  throw new Error('A carousel needs at least 2 slides but the AI returned ' + nSlides +\n    '. Run again. Stopping here costs nothing; carrying on would spend image credits on a post Instagram would reject.');\n}\n\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Brand system. Lives here, in one place, so every frame is identical.\n// The LLM supplies subject matter only -- never colour, style or layout.\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nconst BRAND = [\n  'Design a 3:4 vertical Instagram poster.',\n  '',\n  'BACKGROUND COLOR (non-negotiable, exact, never vary): the entire background is a single flat solid fill of exactly hex #F7F4EC. No gradients, no shading, no texture, no tone variation anywhere in the background - one uniform color, edge to edge.',\n  '',\n  'BRAND SYSTEM (fixed, never vary): flat 2D minimalist vector illustration in an editorial infographic style. Sage green and terracotta orange accents only, with dark forest green for type. Clean geometric shapes, generous white space, no gradients, no photorealism, no 3D, no drop shadows, no paper texture.',\n  '',\n  'NO BORDERS, BOXES OR PLACEHOLDER SHAPES: do not draw any border, frame, card, rectangle, panel, sticky note, tag, badge or placeholder shape anywhere on the poster. The illustration and text sit directly on the flat background with nothing boxed, outlined or bordered.',\n  '',\n  'LAYOUT (strict):',\n  '- SAFE AREA: every piece of text and every important element must sit inside the central safe area, at least 10% of the width in from the left and right edges and at least 12% of the height in from the top and bottom edges (Instagram trims roughly 3% off the top and 3% off the bottom when it displays this frame, so the top and bottom bands must hold nothing that matters). Nothing may touch or bleed off an edge. This poster is viewed as a cropped grid thumbnail, so the headline must be fully readable with room to spare on all four sides.',\n  '- TOP THIRD: the headline. Bold geometric sans-serif, dark forest green, centred, on 1 or 2 lines, set large enough to read at thumbnail size.',\n  '- DIRECTLY UNDER THE HEADLINE: the supporting line. Same sans-serif at a lighter weight, muted grey-green, centred, on 1 or 2 lines, clearly smaller than the headline.',\n  '- LOWER TWO THIRDS: the illustration.',\n   'TYPOGRAPHY: render the two text strings below exactly as written, correctly spelled, with no extra or substituted words. Do not add any other caption, label, date, handle, signature, watermark, page number or decorative filler text. Short functional labels belonging to the diagram itself (arrow labels such as INHALE / EXHALE) are allowed.',\n].join('\\n');\n\nfunction buildPrompt(slide) {\n  return BRAND +\n    '\\n\\nHEADLINE TEXT (exact): \"' + String(slide.headline || '').trim() + '\"' +\n    '\\n\\nSUPPORTING TEXT (exact): \"' + String(slide.sub || '').trim() + '\"' +\n    '\\n\\nILLUSTRATION SUBJECT: ' + String(slide.visual_prompt || '').trim();\n}\n\n// Hard cap on slide count. The agent is *asked* for 3-5 slides, but a prompt is\n// not a constraint, and the output-parser schema can't enforce it either (numeric\n// limits there are runtime validators that hard-fail rather than degrade). Every\n// extra slide is another full-size image rendered downstream, so the ceiling is\n// enforced here, where it actually holds.\nconst MAX_SLIDES = o.post_type === 'CAROUSEL' ? 4 : 1;\n\nconst slides = (o.slides || []).slice(0, MAX_SLIDES).map((s, i) => ({\n  headline: s.headline,\n  sub: s.sub,\n  body: s.body,\n  visual_prompt: s.visual_prompt,\n  slideIndex: i,\n  image_prompt: buildPrompt(s),\n  // Carried on every slide so the image helper workflow needs no editing.\n  s3_bucket_name: settings.s3_bucket_name,\n  s3_region: settings.s3_region,\n}));\n\nif (!slides.length) {\n  throw new Error('AI Agent returned no slides. Raw output: ' + JSON.stringify(o).slice(0, 800));\n}\n\n// Hashtags are kept out of the caption body by the agent, then appended here so\n// the prose block and the tag block stay visually separated in the IG caption.\nconst hashtags = (Array.isArray(o.hashtags) ? o.hashtags : [])\n  .map((h) => String(h).trim())\n  .filter(Boolean)\n  .map((h) => (h.startsWith('#') ? h : '#' + h));\n\nconst caption = [String(o.caption || '').trim(), hashtags.join(' ')]\n  .filter(Boolean)\n  .join('\\n\\n.\\n.\\n.\\n');\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    news_hook: o.news_hook,\n    problem: o.problem,\n    solution: o.solution,\n    practice: o.practice,\n    post_type: o.post_type,\n    caption,\n    hashtags,\n    slides,\n    // Top-level copy for the SINGLE_IMAGE branch, which reaches the renderer\n    // without passing through Split Out Slides.\n    image_prompt: slides[0].image_prompt,\n  },\n}];"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "ec57bbc6-d4d3-48a5-bab6-ccab29014455", "name": "Single or Carousel?", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.switch", "position": [2480, 624], "parameters": {"rules": {"values": [{"outputKey": "single", "conditions": {"options": {"version": 2, "leftValue": "", "caseSensitive": true, "typeValidation": "strict"}, "combinator": "and", "conditions": [{"id": "r-single", "operator": {"type": "string", "operation": "equals"}, "leftValue": "={{ $json.post_type }}", "rightValue": "SINGLE_IMAGE"}]}, "renameOutput": true}, {"outputKey": "carousel", "conditions": {"options": {"version": 2, "leftValue": "", "caseSensitive": true, "typeValidation": "strict"}, "combinator": "and", "conditions": [{"id": "r-carousel", "operator": {"type": "string", "operation": "equals"}, "leftValue": "={{ $json.post_type }}", "rightValue": "CAROUSEL"}]}, "renameOutput": true}]}, "options": {}}, "typeVersion": 3.2}, {"id": "649f88c4-b179-4f24-9738-11d5fc6405fd", "name": "Draw the Picture with Gemini", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [2704, 528], "parameters": {"url": "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/gemini-3-pro-image-preview:generateContent", "method": "POST", "options": {}, "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify( { contents: [ { parts: [ { text: $json.slides[0].image_prompt } ] } ], generationConfig: { imageConfig: { aspectRatio: \"3:4\", imageSize: \"2K\" } } } ) }}", "sendBody": true, "sendHeaders": true, "specifyBody": "json", "authentication": "genericCredentialType", "genericAuthType": "httpQueryAuth", "headerParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}]}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "1dad6805-9807-4fb5-aa9a-9eb0f4d4b7c0", "name": "Prepare Image and Logo", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [2928, 528], "parameters": {"jsCode": "// LOGO: this is a 1x1 transparent placeholder, so no logo is drawn by default.\n// To add yours: make a small PNG (transparent background; bake in any opacity\n// you want), convert it to base64, paste it below, and set LOGO_W / LOGO_H to\n// its size in pixels. It is placed bottom-right with a margin.\nconst LOGO_B64 = 'iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAAC0lEQVR4nGNgAAIAAAUAAXpeqz8AAAAASUVORK5CYII=';\nconst LOGO_W = 1;\nconst LOGO_H = 1;\nconst LOGO_MARGIN_PCT = 0.045;\n\nfunction extractImage(json) {\n  const cands = json.candidates || [];\n  for (const cand of cands) {\n    const parts = (cand.content && cand.content.parts) || [];\n    for (const p of parts) {\n      const inline = p.inlineData || p.inline_data;\n      if (inline && inline.data) {\n        return { data: inline.data, mime: inline.mimeType || inline.mime_type || 'image/png' };\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction extFor(mime) {\n  if (mime.includes('jpeg') || mime.includes('jpg')) return 'jpg';\n  if (mime.includes('webp')) return 'webp';\n  return 'png';\n}\n\n// Read the pixel dimensions straight out of the file header so the watermark can\n// be pinned to the true bottom-right corner whatever size Gemini hands back.\nfunction imageSize(buf) {\n  if (buf.length > 24 && buf[0] === 0x89 && buf[1] === 0x50) {\n    return { width: buf.readUInt32BE(16), height: buf.readUInt32BE(20) };\n  }\n  if (buf.length > 4 && buf[0] === 0xff && buf[1] === 0xd8) {\n    let o = 2;\n    while (o + 9 < buf.length) {\n      if (buf[o] !== 0xff) { o++; continue; }\n      const m = buf[o + 1];\n      if (m === 0x01 || (m >= 0xd0 && m <= 0xd9)) { o += 2; continue; }\n      const len = buf.readUInt16BE(o + 2);\n      const isSOF = m >= 0xc0 && m <= 0xcf && m !== 0xc4 && m !== 0xc8 && m !== 0xcc;\n      if (isSOF) return { height: buf.readUInt16BE(o + 5), width: buf.readUInt16BE(o + 7) };\n      o += 2 + len;\n    }\n  }\n  return { width: 1536, height: 2048 }; // 3:4 @ 2K fallback\n}\n\nfunction describeFailure(json, label) {\n  const cand = (json.candidates || [])[0];\n  const bits = [];\n  if (cand && cand.finishReason) bits.push('finishReason=' + cand.finishReason);\n  if (json.promptFeedback && json.promptFeedback.blockReason) {\n    bits.push('blockReason=' + json.promptFeedback.blockReason);\n  }\n  const textPart = cand && cand.content && (cand.content.parts || []).find(function (p) { return p.text; });\n  if (textPart) bits.push('model returned text instead of an image: ' + textPart.text.slice(0, 300));\n  return 'Gemini returned no image for ' + label + '. ' + bits.join(' | ') +\n    ' | raw: ' + JSON.stringify(json).slice(0, 600);\n}\n\nconst logoBuf = Buffer.from(LOGO_B64, 'base64');\nconst out = [];\nconst items = $input.all();\nconst src = $('Normalize & Plan Slides').first().json;\nconst s3 = $('Your Settings').first().json;\nif (!s3.s3_bucket_name || !s3.s3_region) throw new Error('Fill in s3_bucket_name and s3_region on the \"Your Settings\" node.');\n\nfor (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {\n  const img = extractImage(items[i].json);\n  if (!img) throw new Error(describeFailure(items[i].json, 'single image'));\n\n  const buf = Buffer.from(img.data, 'base64');\n  const dims = imageSize(buf);\n  const margin = Math.round(dims.width * LOGO_MARGIN_PCT);\n  const fileName = `single_${$execution.id}_${i}.${extFor(img.mime)}`;\n\n  const bin = await this.helpers.prepareBinaryData(buf, fileName, img.mime);\n  const logoBin = await this.helpers.prepareBinaryData(logoBuf, 'logo-watermark.png', 'image/png');\n\n  out.push({\n    json: {\n      imageFileName: fileName,\n      imageUrl: `https://${s3.s3_bucket_name}.s3.${s3.s3_region}.amazonaws.com/${fileName}`,\n      caption: src.caption,\n      post_type: src.post_type,\n      imageWidth: dims.width,\n      imageHeight: dims.height,\n      logoX: Math.max(0, dims.width - LOGO_W - margin),\n      logoY: Math.max(0, dims.height - LOGO_H - margin),\n    },\n    binary: { data: bin, logo: logoBin },\n  });\n}\nreturn out;"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "71d542d5-c7de-4ed9-ad9e-aa080a19a65b", "name": "Upload Image to S3", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.s3", "position": [3376, 528], "parameters": {"fileName": "={{ $json.imageFileName }}", "operation": "upload", "bucketName": "={{ $('Your Settings').first().json.s3_bucket_name }}", "additionalFields": {}}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "b558452c-3ca1-42cf-a02d-b5668a1e6586", "name": "Split Out Slides", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.splitOut", "position": [2704, 720], "parameters": {"options": {}, "fieldToSplitOut": "slides"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "c438fbcf-2a72-4b5c-9761-a858af7d795f", "name": "Create Slide Container", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [3152, 720], "parameters": {"url": "=https://graph.facebook.com/v22.0/{{ $('Your Settings').first().json.instagram_business_account_id }}/media", "method": "POST", "options": {}, "sendQuery": true, "authentication": "genericCredentialType", "genericAuthType": "httpQueryAuth", "queryParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "image_url", "value": "={{ $json.imageUrl }}"}, {"name": "is_carousel_item", "value": "true"}]}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "3c3eb90a-22bc-4796-8b3d-2c7daba0bb7f", "name": "Collect Slide Container IDs", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.aggregate", "position": [3376, 720], "parameters": {"options": {}, "aggregate": "aggregateAllItemData", "destinationFieldName": "container_ids"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "e1afd0ce-043d-47c7-a18b-0aa4f49c727a", "name": "Create Carousel Container", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [3600, 720], "parameters": {"url": "=https://graph.facebook.com/v22.0/{{ $('Your Settings').first().json.instagram_business_account_id }}/media", "method": "POST", "options": {}, "sendQuery": true, "authentication": "genericCredentialType", "genericAuthType": "httpQueryAuth", "queryParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "media_type", "value": "CAROUSEL"}, {"name": "children", "value": "={{ $json.container_ids.map(c => c.id || (c.json && c.json.id)).filter(Boolean).join(',') }}"}, {"name": "caption", "value": "={{ $('Normalize & Plan Slides').first().json.caption }}"}]}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "91ab8e22-573f-45af-9baa-4d402cda2c01", "name": "Publish to Instagram", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [4720, 624], "parameters": {"url": "=https://graph.facebook.com/v22.0/{{ $('Your Settings').first().json.instagram_business_account_id }}/media_publish", "method": "POST", "options": {}, "sendQuery": true, "authentication": "genericCredentialType", "genericAuthType": "httpQueryAuth", "queryParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "creation_id", "value": "={{ $('Set Container ID').first().json.container_id }}"}]}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "3aea26ff-c130-41ac-852e-bff29c6315f5", "name": "Wait for Container", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.wait", "position": [4048, 720], "webhookId": "c4e81f37-52a9-4d6b-8e10-3f7b2a95d8c1", "parameters": {"amount": 15}, "typeVersion": 1.1}, {"id": "7bb2a4c8-4234-4057-ad26-7e8298d96d1b", "name": "Check Container Status", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [4272, 640], "parameters": {"url": "=https://graph.facebook.com/v22.0/{{ $('Set Container ID').first().json.container_id }}", "options": {}, "sendQuery": true, "authentication": "genericCredentialType", "genericAuthType": "httpQueryAuth", "queryParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "fields", "value": "status_code,status"}]}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "1ef44029-34a6-42d5-8d61-9d00569b0381", "name": "Container Status Router", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.switch", "position": [4496, 688], "parameters": {"rules": {"values": [{"outputKey": "ready", "conditions": {"options": {"version": 2, "leftValue": "", "caseSensitive": true, "typeValidation": "strict"}, "combinator": "and", "conditions": [{"id": "r-ready", "operator": {"type": "string", "operation": "equals"}, "leftValue": "={{ $json.status_code }}", "rightValue": "FINISHED"}]}, "renameOutput": true}, {"outputKey": "failed", "conditions": {"options": {"version": 2, "leftValue": "", "caseSensitive": true, "typeValidation": "strict"}, "combinator": "and", "conditions": [{"id": "r-error", "operator": {"type": "string", "operation": "equals"}, "leftValue": "={{ $json.status_code }}", "rightValue": "ERROR"}]}, "renameOutput": true}, {"outputKey": "timeout", "conditions": {"options": {"version": 2, "leftValue": "", "caseSensitive": true, "typeValidation": "strict"}, "combinator": "and", "conditions": [{"id": "r-timeout", "operator": {"type": "number", "operation": "gte"}, "leftValue": "={{ $runIndex }}", "rightValue": 12}]}, "renameOutput": true}]}, "options": {"fallbackOutput": "extra"}}, "typeVersion": 3.2}, {"id": "b30fed0f-2624-48a0-997b-493f39cecbd6", "name": "Container Not Publishable", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stopAndError", "position": [4720, 816], "parameters": {"errorMessage": "=Carousel container {{ $('Set Container ID').first().json.container_id }} never became publishable (status_code={{ $json.status_code }}, status={{ $json.status }}) after {{ $runIndex + 1 }} checks."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "ffbc0933-41c8-4644-82b4-06273f987564", "name": "Add Logo", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.editImage", "position": [3152, 528], "parameters": {"options": {}, "operation": "composite", "positionX": "={{ $json.logoX }}", "positionY": "={{ $json.logoY }}", "dataPropertyNameComposite": "logo"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "18c22360-d49f-4dbf-8d42-af76cd46e128", "name": "Anthropic Chat Model", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatAnthropic", "position": [1904, 848], "parameters": {"model": {"__rl": true, "mode": "id", "value": "claude-sonnet-5"}, "options": {"maxTokensToSample": 8192}}, "credentials": {"anthropicApi": {"id": "72a50b4450644155", "name": "Dummy anthropicApi"}}, "typeVersion": 1.3}, {"id": "4547a244-b061-4a3c-8247-80ddb9d07d72", "name": "Make Slide Image (helper workflow)", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflow", "position": [2928, 720], "parameters": {"mode": "each", "options": {"waitForSubWorkflow": true}, "workflowId": {"__rl": true, "mode": "list", "value": "", "cachedResultName": ""}}, "typeVersion": 1.2}, {"id": "77c84eb7-aca5-4005-bbee-298b6488a1bd", "name": "Create Single Post Container", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [3600, 528], "parameters": {"url": "=https://graph.facebook.com/v22.0/{{ $('Your Settings').first().json.instagram_business_account_id }}/media", "method": "POST", "options": {}, "sendQuery": true, "authentication": "genericCredentialType", "genericAuthType": "httpQueryAuth", "queryParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "image_url", "value": "={{ $('Prepare Image and Logo').first().json.imageUrl }}"}, {"name": "caption", "value": "={{ $('Normalize & Plan Slides').first().json.caption }}"}]}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "8804866c-8219-4598-8c40-44c8011f34f7", "name": "Set Container ID", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set", "position": [3824, 624], "parameters": {"options": {}, "assignments": {"assignments": [{"id": "6888e292-58d2-460a-a842-493584ccd575", "name": "container_id", "type": "string", "value": "={{ $json.id }}"}]}}, "typeVersion": 3.4}, {"id": "15ddd8fd-b999-4632-865f-2ee20cc48939", "name": "Your Settings", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set", "position": [1008, 624], "parameters": {"options": {}, "assignments": {"assignments": [{"id": "93c8f91f-6c98-462e-aedc-1d8d5ee3bbd1", "name": "instagram_business_account_id", "type": "string", "value": "YOUR_INSTAGRAM_BUSINESS_ACCOUNT_ID"}, {"id": "32ecaa99-00ec-4a7d-bcd9-cf43be5c7b50", "name": "s3_bucket_name", "type": "string", "value": "your-bucket-name"}, {"id": "588c4003-f557-42e4-bb5a-2ed5397ac568", "name": "s3_region", "type": "string", "value": "us-east-1"}, {"id": "1f9cdeca-2609-49ba-99fd-903776cc746b", "name": "post_type_mode", "type": "string", "value": "AUTO"}]}}, "typeVersion": 3.4}, {"id": "8215f022-ea99-42af-b98d-5b39a35a3a20", "name": "Sticky Description", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [16, 144], "parameters": {"width": 700, "height": 1604, "content": "# \ud83d\udcf8 A daily Instagram post (single & carousel), written and drawn for you with an automatic posting\n\nThis daily workflow pulls trending headlines from Google News RSS, uses Anthropic Claude to write an Instagram caption and slide copy, generates matching images with Google Gemini, uploads assets to Amazon S3, and publishes either a single-image post or a carousel to Instagram via the Facebook Graph API.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f **There is no approval step.** Once the workflow is active it posts on its own.\nTest with it switched off and check the first few posts carefully.\n\n\ud83d\udc64 Who is it for\n\n- anyone running an Instagram **Business or Creator** account who wants a steady\n  stream of on-brand posts without designing each one\n- it is written for a **yoga and mindfulness** page, but the topics and the tone\n  are just text you can change (see *How to customize*)\n\n**Not for you if** you want real photos, or want to approve every post first.\n\n### \u2699\ufe0f How it works\n\n1. Runs every 24 hours on a schedule.\n2. Rotates through a predefined set of topic-based Google News RSS feeds and fetches the top headlines.\n3. Builds a short news context from the top three articles and sends it to Anthropic Claude to select one headline and generate the post caption, hashtags, and slide plan (single image or carousel).\n4. Normalizes the AI output, enforces the configured post type, and turns each slide into a branded image prompt.\n5. Generates images with the Google Gemini image model, optionally composites a logo, and uploads the image files to an Amazon S3 bucket to produce public image URLs.\n6. Creates an Instagram media container (single image or carousel) using the Facebook Graph API, polls until the container is finished, and publishes the post to the connected Instagram business account.\n\n\n### \ud83d\udee0 How to set up (about 6 hours the first time)\n1. Add an Anthropic API credential for Claude.\n2. Add a Google Gemini API key as an HTTP Query Auth credential and ensure the Gemini image endpoint is enabled for your project.\n3. Add an Instagram/Facebook Graph API access token (HTTP Query Auth) with permission to publish content and set your Instagram business account ID in the workflow settings.\n4. Configure Amazon S3 credentials, create an S3 bucket that allows public reads for uploaded images, and fill in the bucket name and region in the settings.\n5. Import and select the required helper workflow in the \u201cMake Slide Image (helper workflow)\u201d step for carousel rendering, and optionally replace the placeholder base64 logo in the image preparation step.\n\n### \ud83d\udccb Requirements\n\nAnthropic, Google Gemini (image model), an Instagram Business/Creator account\nconnected to a Facebook Page, and an AWS S3 bucket. Each run costs a little: AI\nwriting plus one Gemini image per slide. While testing, use `SINGLE_IMAGE`.\n\n** This template comes in two parts.\nImport **\u201cDraw and upload one Instagram slide image with Gemini\u201d** as well. Then open the\n**Make Slide Image (helper workflow)** node here and choose it from the dropdown.\n\n\n\n### Customizations\n\nYou can customize the topic to your choice and set type of post you want (single , carousel)\n\n### \ud83c\udfa8 How to customize\n\n- **Topics and news sources:** edit the list in **Pick the Daily Topic**\n- **Look of the pictures** (colours, style, layout): one place only,\n  **Normalize & Plan Slides**\n- **Voice and rules for the writing:** the prompts in **Write the Post with Claude**\n- **Time of day:** the **Schedule Trigger**\n- **Your logo:** see the note on **Prepare Image and Logo*\n\n\n### Additional information\n\n**- Prepare the S3 bucket.** Instagram downloads each picture from a public web\naddress, so the bucket must allow public reads of its files (a bucket policy).\n\n**- Fill in \u201cYour Settings\u201d** (the node right after the clock):\n- `instagram_business_account_id` \u2014 your Instagram account\u2019s numeric id\n- `s3_bucket_name` and `s3_region` \u2014 the bucket, and its region (`us-east-1` \u2026)\n- `post_type_mode` \u2014 `AUTO`, `SINGLE_IMAGE` or `CAROUSEL`\n\n\n\n"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "49e8d673-2082-45e2-b90b-b165bce0da96", "name": "Sticky Step 1", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [944, 480], "parameters": {"color": "#E0F002", "width": 892, "height": 300, "content": "### \ud83d\udd58 Step 1 \u2014 Wake up, pick a topic, read the news\n\n**Your Settings** \u2014 the only node you *must* fill in.\n**Pick the Daily Topic** \u2014 chooses today\u2019s topic from four, in rotation, and the news feed to read.\n**Fetch News Headlines / Build News Context** \u2014 read the feed and keep the top three headlines.\n\n**Good to know:** the rotation only moves forward when the workflow runs as an *active*\n(scheduled) workflow. In manual test runs n8n does not save it, so a test always picks the first topic."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "7b64251b-ad94-40ec-915a-abcc736912dc", "name": "Sticky Step 2", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1872, 448], "parameters": {"color": "#E0F000", "width": 556, "height": 300, "content": "### \u270d\ufe0f Step 2 \u2014 Write the post and plan the pictures\n\n**Write the Post with Claude** \u2014 picks the strongest headline and writes the caption, hashtags and slides.\n**Post Output Parser** \u2014 makes Claude answer in a fixed shape; a bad answer is retried up to 3 times.\n**Normalize & Plan Slides** \u2014 the art director. Owns the whole visual style and turns each slide into a finished image prompt. **To change the look, change it here.**"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "4da7c5d7-a993-408d-976b-ae652f196fbc", "name": "Sticky Step 3", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [2448, 272], "parameters": {"color": "#E0F000", "width": 1052, "height": 668, "content": "### \ud83c\udfa8 Step 3 \u2014 Draw and upload the pictures\n\n**Single or Carousel?** sends the post down one of two paths.\n**Single path:** draw with Gemini \u2192 add your logo \u2192 upload to S3.\n**Carousel path:** each slide goes to the **helper workflow**, one at a time, then comes back as a small web address.\n**Why one at a time?** n8n keeps everything it has done in memory until a run ends. Images are big; four at once can crash a run.\n**Sometimes Gemini declines to draw.** The run then stops with an error and nothing is published \u2014 just run it again."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "21a20609-b18c-4911-a91c-a379bb1464f1", "name": "Sticky Step 4", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [3568, 416], "parameters": {"color": "#E0F000", "width": 1500, "height": 580, "content": "### \ud83d\ude80 Step 4 \u2014 Publish to Instagram\n\nInstagram publishes in two steps: **make a container** (the post, prepared), then **publish it**.\nBoth paths end in the same place: **Set Container ID \u2192 Wait \u2192 Check Container Status \u2192 Publish to Instagram**.\nThe check repeats every 15 seconds (up to 12 times) until Instagram says the container is `FINISHED`; an `ERROR` or a timeout stops the run with a clear message."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "f128245a-8cb1-43d8-bff6-e3ef442f817e", "name": "Sticky Setup Warning", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [3136, 1040], "parameters": {"color": 3, "width": 560, "height": 260, "content": "## \u26a0\ufe0f For generating carousel images a sub-workflow is there which is not a part of this workflow. It can be accessed with the name - 'Sub-render for Instagram images and carousels from live news with Claude and Gemini' in my creator profile\n\n"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "webhook-automata-injected-1791111459412", "name": "Automata Webhook", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook", "position": [0, 0], "webhookId": "r3K6AOqHSQD6ceXL", "parameters": {"path": "r3K6AOqHSQD6ceXL", "options": {}, "httpMethod": "POST", "responseCode": 200, "responseMode": "onReceived"}, "typeVersion": 1.1}]
