pify freelancers"}]}}, "typeVersion": 3.4}, {"id": "17a08492-f295-4e94-9693-755733b684a3", "name": "Edit Fields5", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set", "position": [12000, 5056], "parameters": {"options": {}, "assignments": {"assignments": [{"id": "db8c7ce8-6a1a-4744-bd7c-114ef186fee4", "name": "topic", "type": "string", "value": "shopify"}]}}, "typeVersion": 3.4}, {"id": "69fcbcd6-f4c9-46c4-926b-ba02816dcbfd", "name": "Edit Fields6", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set", "position": [12000, 5248], "parameters": {"options": {}, "assignments": {"assignments": [{"id": "d91901ce-d7bc-448d-a2de-7cdd8e42e745", "name": "topic", "type": "string", "value": "Search Engine Optimization"}]}}, "typeVersion": 3.4}, {"id": "977eee3c-73f9-4fea-bc44-de26815fc13a", "name": "Convert to File", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.convertToFile", "position": [14400, 4672], "parameters": {"options": {}, "operation": "toBinary", "sourceProperty": "candidates[0].content.parts[0].inlineData.data"}, "typeVersion": 1.1}, {"id": "54f74745-08e0-43c5-b083-5a7445c5fdb6", "name": "Generating Post Content", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent", "position": [13248, 4672], "parameters": {"text": "=You are an expert storyteller and LinkedIn content strategist. Your task is to turn the following summary into a compelling, easy-to-read story for a broad audience.\n\nSummary to Use:\n{{ $json.data }}\n\nPost Requirements:\n\nStart with a strong hook based on the formula: Hook Score = (Curiosity x Relevance x Specificity) - Friction.\nCuriosity: Make them need to know what happens next.\nRelevance: Map it exactly to their situation.\nSpecificity: Use real numbers, names, and outcomes over vague claims.\nFriction: Strip out abstract or clich\u00e9 openers (e.g., standard \"5 lessons I learned\" templates).\nWrite so a 15-year-old can understand (easy words, short sentences).\nAvoid sounding like generic AI. The post must sound like an actual person with actual receipts\u2014sharp, human-edited, and authentic.\nFocus on a specific pain point and transition smoothly into the value or solution.\nKeep a casual and warm tone.\nMake it 250-350 words long.\nEnd with a soft, value-driven, open-ended question that creates zero burden or commitment for the reader to answer.\nDo not use asterisks (*) or hashtags.\n\n\nOUTPUT RULE - IMPORTANT - DON'T MISS:\n\nYour response must ONLY be the raw text of the LinkedIn post. Do not add any titles, labels, or explanations. Just the post itself.", "options": {}, "promptType": "define", "hasOutputParser": true}, "typeVersion": 1.7}, {"id": "b533446b-af84-4ac7-8ae9-235667349ec0", "name": "Google Gemini Chat Model2", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini", "position": [13792, 4880], "parameters": {"options": {}, "modelName": "models/gemini-flash-latest"}, "credentials": {"googlePalmApi": {"id": "11a68a950433485d", "name": "Dummy googlePalmApi"}}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "bca1ebc2-16a6-415b-a9a1-8a9d668529cf", "name": "HTTP Request1", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [14176, 4672], "parameters": {"url": "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image:generateContent", "method": "POST", "options": {}, "jsonBody": "={\n  \"contents\": [\n    {\n      \"parts\": [\n        { \"text\": \"{{ $json.output }}\" }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"generationConfig\": {\n    \"responseModalities\": [\"IMAGE\"],\n    \"imageConfig\": {\n      \"aspectRatio\": \"16:9\",\n      \"imageSize\": \"1K\"\n    }\n  }\n}", "sendBody": true, "specifyBody": "json", "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType", "nodeCredentialType": "googlePalmApi"}, "retryOnFail": false, "typeVersion": 4.2, "waitBetweenTries": 5000}, {"id": "8788fe59-663f-4fd8-a5da-a82243e147da", "name": "Image Generation", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent", "position": [13824, 4672], "parameters": {"text": "=Read following Social Media post which I have generated. And write a prompt to generate image which looks good, does not have much Character/Words. \n\n# INSTRUCTIONS:\n1- Don't include any special characters in prompt.\n2- Don't include any comma or inverted comma\n3- Only a return text based prompt for image generation\n\n# SOCIAL MEDIA POST:\n{{ $json.output }}", "options": {}, "promptType": "define"}, "typeVersion": 1.9}, {"id": "c990c41e-47df-4760-88fa-2d5ee6e8bfc1", "name": "Choose Best Artcile", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent", "position": [12448, 4672], "parameters": {"text": "=You are an expert **tech** social media strategist and content curator. Your mission is to analyze the following articles and select the SINGLE best **tech-related** article with the highest potential for social media engagement.\n\n**Input Articles:**\n\nArticle #1:\nTitle: {{ $json.results[0].title }}\nDescription: {{ $json.results[0].description }}\nURL: {{ $json.results[0].link }}\n\nArticle #2:\nTitle: {{ $json.results[1].title }}\nDescription: {{ $json.results[1].description }}\nURL: {{ $json.results[1].link }}\n\nArticle #3:\nTitle: {{ $json.results[2].title }}\nDescription: {{ $json.results[2].description }}\nURL: {{ $json.results[2].link }}\n\n**Your Selection Process:**\n\n**Step 1: The Tech Filter (Primary Requirement)**\nFirst, determine which of the articles are primarily about technology. This includes topics like software development, AI, cybersecurity, hardware, SaaS, gadgets, data science, or the tech industry itself. An article is only eligible if it passes this filter.\n\n**Step 2: Social Potential Analysis (Secondary Requirement)**\nFrom the pool of **eligible tech articles**, evaluate them against these criteria to find the single best one:\n    *   **Curiosity Gap:** Does the title make people curious to know more?\n    *   **Value Proposition:** Does it promise a clear solution, benefit, or valuable insight for a tech audience?\n    *   **Emotional Hook:** Does it tap into a strong emotion relevant to professionals (e.g., inspiration, frustration with a common problem, excitement about innovation)?\n\n**Step 3: Make the Final Selection**\nChoose the one article that best meets the criteria from Step 1 and Step 2.\n\n**Fallback Rule:** If NONE of the articles are clearly about technology, then and only then should you disregard the tech filter and select the single article with the highest overall social potential from the original list.\n\n**Final Output Instructions (CRITICAL):**\n*   Your response must ONLY contain information for the single article you chose.\n*   Write a BRAND NEW summary. This summary must be under 100 words and rewritten to be compelling for social media, highlighting why someone should click. Do NOT just copy the original description.\n*   Do not include any explanation of your choice or mention the other articles.", "options": {"returnIntermediateSteps": false}, "promptType": "define", "hasOutputParser": true}, "typeVersion": 1.7}, {"id": "46d109a2-ec1f-47c6-96a8-9d01837ba099", "name": "HTTP Request2", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [13024, 4672], "parameters": {"url": "=https://r.jina.ai/{{ $json.output.url }}", "options": {}, "sendHeaders": true, "headerParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE"}]}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "87ba37e7-56f7-4d4d-99a7-286059ffd127", "name": "Structured Output Parser", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured", "position": [12592, 4896], "parameters": {"jsonSchemaExample": "{\n\t\"title\": \"This is the title of article\",\n  \t\"url\": \"https://example.com\",\n    \"summary\": \"This is the summary of the article, which should be with in maximum 100 words\"\n}"}, "typeVersion": 1.2}, {"id": "464d7c18-0bb4-4c8f-8114-983ca01df6ac", "name": "Send a message", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack", "position": [14672, 4800], "webhookId": "73d4ded9-0cd7-4261-a8af-e6a22625b75b", "parameters": {"user": {"__rl": true, "mode": "list", "value": "UFK9SGZE3", "cachedResultUrl": "", "cachedResultName": "Bilal Naseer (@bilalnaseer01)"}, "message": "=Please approve or disapprove following content:\n\n {{ $('Generating Post Content').item.json.output }}", "options": {"limitWaitTime": {"values": {"resumeUnit": "minutes", "resumeAmount": 30}}}, "operation": "sendAndWait", "approvalOptions": {"values": {"approvalType": "double"}}}, "typeVersion": 2.4}, {"id": "08ee0d21-c433-4b09-8a35-07f9a58f3a74", "name": "If", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if", "position": [14880, 4800], "parameters": {"options": {}, "conditions": {"options": {"version": 3, "leftValue": "", "caseSensitive": true, "typeValidation": "strict"}, "combinator": "and", "conditions": [{"id": "ca40b71b-5d42-4c69-84cc-36b36e2471a8", "operator": {"type": "boolean", "operation": "true", "singleValue": true}, "leftValue": "={{ $json.data.approved }}", "rightValue": ""}]}}, "typeVersion": 2.3}, {"id": "701cb53a-9776-48f1-b374-340a6533e469", "name": "No Operation, do nothing", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp", "position": [15216, 4928], "parameters": {}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "93df245b-8b4f-4355-a039-1f2631944921", "name": "Code in JavaScript", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [15184, 4656], "parameters": {"jsCode": "// Fetch the item from the \"Convert to File\" node\nconst fileNode = $items(\"Convert to File\")[0];\n\n// Attach the binary image back to the current item\n$input.item.binary = {\n  data: fileNode.binary.data\n};\n\nreturn $input.item;"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "ece5412a-a8bf-40d8-8d7d-0c5e071eef96", "name": "Create a post1", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.linkedIn", "position": [15472, 4752], "parameters": {"text": "={{ $('Wait').item.json.output }}", "person": "Hq26b0Pv2u", "additionalFields": {}, "shareMediaCategory": "IMAGE"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "webhook-automata-injected-1791111459394", "name": "Automata Webhook", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook", "position": [0, 0], "webhookId": "n0Ifv0ePnfwFxb7o", "parameters": {"path": "n0Ifv0ePnfwFxb7o", "options": {}, "httpMethod": "POST", "responseCode": 200, "responseMode": "onReceived"}, "typeVersion": 1.1}]
F3h54irwGJxhM2yU|[{"id": "7ffd5c10-6afc-4082-80a1-ba4bf494f58b", "name": "Sticky Note", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [528, 544], "parameters": {"width": 560, "height": 980, "content": "## Customer Support Triage & SLA Calendar Dispatcher\n\nAutomate incoming customer inquiry triage from Gmail with Google Gemini. The system classifies requests, calculates dynamic SLA deadlines based on urgency, schedules follow-up blocks in Google Calendar, logs ticket records in Google Sheets, generates AI reply drafts, and sends instant Discord alerts for high-priority incidents.\n\nWho's it for: Customer support leads, IT service desks, and operations teams needing automated triage and SLA tracking without manual data entry.\n\n### How it works\n1. When Email Arrives polls unread emails with the subject \"Inquiry Received\".\n2. Language Model Processing and Gemini parse the email body into structured JSON (priority, category, summary, draft).\n3. Calculate SLA & Deadlines computes resolution target times (High: 4h, Medium: 1 day, Low: 3 days).\n4. Add to Google Calendar creates a deadline block, Append Details to Sheets logs the record, and Create Gmail Draft saves a reply.\n5. If priority is High, Check Priority Level routes a critical alert to Send Urgent Discord Alert.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect your Gmail, Google Gemini, Google Calendar, and Google Sheets credentials.\n2. Prepare a Google Sheet titled `form` with headers: received_at, priority, category, sender, subject, summary, deadline, calendar_event_url.\n3. Configure your Discord Webhook URL in Send Urgent Discord Alert.\n\n### Customization tips\n- Adjust dynamic SLA hours directly in the JavaScript code inside Calculate SLA & Deadlines.\n- Modify the prompt in Language Model Processing to adapt categorization tags to your domain."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "fb7737b5-91a9-4055-adb5-846f738db3bb", "name": "Sticky Note1", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1152, 640], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 576, "height": 528, "content": "## 1. Receive and classify email\n\nCaptures new support emails from Gmail and uses the LLM chain, Gemini chat model, and structured parser to extract triage details in a predictable format."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "29e8d2f4-9b4d-4731-b52a-43897c618700", "name": "Sticky Note2", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1760, 576], "parameters": {"color": 7, "height": 384, "content": "## 2. Calculate SLA deadlines\n\nUses custom code to convert the structured triage output into SLA dates, deadlines, and priority metadata before splitting into downstream actions."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "bfa71d6d-87bb-42fa-84b0-0f4e9f0f65b8", "name": "Sticky Note3", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [2032, 544], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 672, "height": 320, "content": "## 3. Schedule and draft response\n\nCreates a Google Calendar item for the SLA follow-up, logs the triaged case in Google Sheets, and prepares a Gmail draft response for the support team."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "3e0a6b69-a4d9-4c81-a696-27ff6a705c4f", "name": "Sticky Note4", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1888, 1056], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 496, "height": 320, "content": "## 4. Send urgent alerts\n\nChecks whether the calculated priority meets the urgent criteria and sends a Discord notification for cases that need immediate attention."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "52442285-2764-4448-bb68-ec21d13ca212", "name": "When Email Arrives", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmailTrigger", "position": [1200, 800], "parameters": {"filters": {"q": "subject:\"Inquiry Received\"", "readStatus": "unread"}, "pollTimes": {"item": [{"mode": "everyMinute"}]}}, "typeVersion": 1.1}, {"id": "93ba0cca-4034-4ca1-be14-a69a88f25487", "name": "Language Model Processing", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm", "position": [1424, 800], "parameters": {"text": "=Please analyze the following incoming customer inquiry email and return the result strictly in the specified JSON schema.\n\n[Sender]: {{ $json.from?.text || $json.from?.value?.[0]?.address || $json.from || '' }}\n[Subject]: {{ $json.subject || '' }}\n[Body]: {{ $json.text || $json.snippet || '' }}", "promptType": "define", "hasOutputParser": true}, "typeVersion": 1.5}, {"id": "943fd210-b232-4263-abe1-1ff5550ba02e", "name": "Gemini AI Conversation", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini", "position": [1344, 1024], "parameters": {"options": {}}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "5c1b7355-acca-406f-8ad2-c41a157edd3f", "name": "Parse Structured Output", "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured", "position": [1504, 1024], "parameters": {"schemaType": "manual", "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"category\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Category of inquiry: Billing, Technical, Account, or Other\"\n    },\n    \"priority\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"High\", \"Medium\", \"Low\"],\n      \"description\": \"Urgency level of the customer email\"\n    },\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Concise summary of the inquiry within 1-2 sentences\"\n    },\n    \"reply_draft\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Professional and polite email reply draft\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"category\",\n    \"priority\",\n    \"summary\",\n    \"reply_draft\"\n  ]\n}"}, "typeVersion": 1.2}, {"id": "32c45b12-1d9d-4775-a1d8-dc10a0c8f2c0", "name": "Calculate SLA & Deadlines", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [1808, 800], "parameters": {"jsCode": "const item = $input.first().json;\nconst gmail = $('When Email Arrives').first().json;\n\n// Extract structured outputs from LangChain node\nconst priority = item.output?.priority || item.priority || 'Medium';\nconst category = item.output?.category || item.category || 'General Inquiry';\nconst summary = item.output?.summary || item.summary || '';\nconst replyDraft = item.output?.reply_draft || item.reply_draft || '';\n\n// Robust extraction for sender and subject\nconst sender = \n  gmail.from?.text || \n  gmail.from?.value?.[0]?.address || \n  gmail.From || \n  gmail.from || \n  gmail.sender || \n  '';\n\nconst subject = \n  gmail.subject || \n  gmail.Subject || \n  'Customer Inquiry';\n\nconst threadId = gmail.threadId || gmail.thread_id || '';\nconst messageId = gmail.id || '';\n\nconst now = new Date();\nlet deadline = new Date(now);\n\n// Dynamic SLA Logic\nif (priority === 'High') {\n  deadline.setHours(deadline.getHours() + 4);\n} else if (priority === 'Medium') {\n  deadline.setDate(deadline.getDate() + 1);\n  deadline.setHours(18, 0, 0, 0);\n} else {\n  deadline.setDate(deadline.getDate() + 3);\n  deadline.setHours(18, 0, 0, 0);\n}\n\n// Format local date string (JST)\nconst formatLocalDate = (date) => {\n  const pad = (n) => String(n).padStart(2, '0');\n  return `${date.getFullYear()}-${pad(date.getMonth() + 1)}-${pad(date.getDate())} ${pad(date.getHours())}:${pad(date.getMinutes())}:${pad(date.getSeconds())}`;\n};\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    priority: priority,\n    category: category,\n    summary: summary,\n    replyDraft: replyDraft,\n    sender: sender,\n    subject: subject,\n    threadId: threadId,\n    messageId: messageId,\n    startTime: now.toISOString(),\n    deadlineTime: deadline.toISOString(),\n    deadlineDisplay: formatLocalDate(deadline),\n    taskTitle: `[Action Required / ${priority}] ${category}: ${subject}`\n  }\n}];"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "e6cbcbc8-c351-401d-a850-fd45c0532db8", "name": "Add to Google Calendar", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleCalendar", "position": [2080, 704], "parameters": {"end": "={{ $json.deadlineTime }}", "start": "={{ $json.startTime }}", "calendar": {"__rl": true, "mode": "list", "value": "primary", "cachedResultName": "primary"}, "additionalFields": {"summary": "={{ $json.taskTitle }}", "description": "=【Inquiry Summary】\n{{ $json.summary }}\n\n【Priority & SLA】\nPriority: {{ $json.priority }}\nDeadline: {{ $json.deadlineDisplay }}\n\n【Ticket Details】\nSender: {{ $json.sender }}\nSubject: {{ $json.subject }}\nThread ID: {{ $json.threadId }}"}}, "typeVersion": 1.2}, {"id": "cdc6eaf4-d10f-4c1b-9892-38faffcff5b8", "name": "Append Details to Sheets", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets", "position": [2320, 704], "parameters": {"columns": {"value": {"sender": "={{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.sender }}", "subject": "={{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.subject }}", "summary": "={{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.summary }}", "category": "={{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.category }}", "deadline": "={{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.deadlineDisplay }}", "priority": "={{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.priority }}", "received_at": "={{ $now.toFormat('yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss') }}", "calendar_event_url": "={{ $json.htmlLink || '' }}"}, "mappingMode": "defineBelow"}, "options": {}, "operation": "append", "sheetName": {"__rl": true, "mode": "name", "value": "YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEETS_NAME"}, "documentId": {"__rl": true, "mode": "id", "value": "YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEETS_ID"}}, "typeVersion": 4.5}, {"id": "38488330-c559-42fa-b24c-a98d5f6c7e47", "name": "Create Gmail Draft", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail", "position": [2560, 704], "webhookId": "db8109dd-02af-4df0-ab49-2a98cdab56e0", "parameters": {"message": "={{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.replyDraft }}", "options": {"threadId": "={{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.threadId }}"}, "subject": "=Re: {{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.subject }}", "resource": "draft"}, "typeVersion": 2.1}, {"id": "e64f79d7-ef1f-4342-9dcc-ce9eb9bf17b4", "name": "Check Priority Level", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if", "position": [1936, 1232], "parameters": {"options": {}, "conditions": {"options": {"version": 2, "leftValue": "", "caseSensitive": true, "typeValidation": "strict"}, "combinator": "and", "conditions": [{"id": "priority-high-condition", "operator": {"type": "string", "operation": "equals"}, "leftValue": "={{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.priority }}", "rightValue": "High"}]}}, "typeVersion": 2.2}, {"id": "65f503b8-62e6-4cc3-8888-22de57ce905f", "name": "Send Urgent Discord Alert", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.discord", "position": [2240, 1216], "webhookId": "cafcef01-93d0-4b71-86f6-83f344cfae92", "parameters": {"content": "=🚨 **[Critical Customer Alert / High Priority]**\n\n- **Deadline**: {{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.deadlineDisplay }}\n- **Category**: {{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.category }}\n- **Sender**: {{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.sender }}\n- **Subject**: {{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.subject }}\n\n**Summary**:\n{{ $('Calculate SLA & Deadlines').item.json.summary }}\n\n*(Draft reply has been generated in Gmail. Please verify immediately.)*", "options": {}, "authentication": "webhook"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "webhook-automata-injected-1791111459406", "name": "Automata Webhook", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook", "position": [0, 0], "webhookId": "F3h54irwGJxhM2yU", "parameters": {"path": "F3h54irwGJxhM2yU", "options": {}, "httpMethod": "POST", "responseCode": 200, "responseMode": "onReceived"}, "typeVersion": 1.1}]
1dSFJgL340NlOBkh|[{"id": "b20161b9-009c-4670-9563-377582851b77", "name": "Sticky Note", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [-1152, 96], "parameters": {"width": 800, "height": 800, "content": "## Real-time threat detection & incident response\n\nScans and aggregates threat intelligence, network logs, and vulnerability data every 15 minutes to detect emerging risks across the infrastructure. Detected threats are scored by severity \u2014 critical and high issues trigger immediate multi-channel alerts and incident tickets, while medium and low threats are logged for trend analysis. Every scan closes with an executive summary posted to Slack.\n\n## How it works\n\n1. **Collect** \u2014 Fetches network logs from SIEM, vulnerability scan results, and external threat intel feeds in parallel\n2. **Merge & analyze** \u2014 Combines all data, then detects brute force attacks, malware, critical CVEs, suspicious traffic, and IOC matches\n3. **Route by severity** \u2014 Critical/High threats go to immediate alerting; Medium/Low are logged to the database\n4. **Alert** \u2014 Sends Slack alert, detailed email to SOC, creates a PagerDuty incident, and opens a ticket\n5. **Log** \u2014 Stores Medium/Low threats to SIEM and PostgreSQL for audit trail\n6. **Report** \u2014 Merges all paths and posts a scan summary to the Slack monitoring channel\n\n## Setup steps\n\n1. **SIEM** \u2014 Replace `your-siem-system.com` with your SIEM endpoint in both the log fetch and log write nodes\n2. **Vulnerability scanner** \u2014 Update the scanner URL and replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your credentials\n3. **Threat intel** \u2014 Add your API key to the threat intelligence feed node header\n4. **PagerDuty** \u2014 Replace `YOUR_PAGERDUTY_KEY` and `YOUR_SERVICE_ID` in the PagerDuty node\n5. **Ticketing** \u2014 Update the ticket URL to your Jira or ServiceNow instance and add `YOUR_TICKET_API_KEY`\n6. **Slack** \u2014 Set the correct channel IDs in both Slack nodes (alerts channel and monitoring channel)\n7. **Email** \u2014 Configure SMTP credentials; update `from` and `to` addresses in the email node\n8. **PostgreSQL** \u2014 Ensure a `threat_log` table exists with columns: severity, type, description, timestamp, action_required"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "7c9fbfd3-9663-4ad2-84d2-2dc19cf804da", "name": "Sticky Note1", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [-176, 144], "parameters": {"color": 4, "width": 440, "height": 876, "content": "## 1. Data collection\n\nTriggers every 15 minutes and fetches network logs, vulnerability scan results, and external threat intelligence feeds in parallel before merging them for analysis."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "34565425-c656-4881-928d-32f678ac9cdf", "name": "Sticky Note2", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [304, 352], "parameters": {"color": 4, "width": 436, "height": 460, "content": "## 2. Threat analysis\n\nMerges all collected data and runs detection logic to identify brute force attacks, malware signatures, critical vulnerabilities, suspicious traffic patterns, and IOC matches. Each threat is tagged with a severity level."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "d929174b-463e-4376-89f0-5a63f282b7f8", "name": "Sticky Note3", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [800, 256], "parameters": {"color": 4, "width": 640, "height": 860, "content": "## 3. Alert & remediate\n\nCritical and High threats trigger a Slack alert, a detailed SOC email, a PagerDuty incident, and an incident ticket. Medium and Low threats are logged to SIEM and stored in PostgreSQL."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "0a3e7f2b-d06f-45fb-a8dd-33125071246a", "name": "Sticky Note4", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1488, 336], "parameters": {"color": 4, "width": 764, "height": 524, "content": "## 4. Summary report\n\nAll paths merge and a scan summary \u2014 total threats by severity and type \u2014 is posted to the Slack monitoring channel after every run."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "5633b4a5-b9cf-44ea-99ea-0dad8156574c", "name": "Schedule Trigger - Every 15 Minutes", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger", "position": [-144, 496], "parameters": {"rule": {"interval": [{"field": "minutes", "minutesInterval": 15}]}}, "typeVersion": 1.2}, {"id": "9de6147c-8a55-4613-913a-604093822d75", "name": "Fetch Network Logs", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [96, 384], "parameters": {"url": "https://your-siem-system.com/api/logs", "method": "POST", "options": {}, "sendBody": true, "sendHeaders": true, "bodyParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "time_range", "value": "15m"}, {"name": "log_types", "value": "firewall,ids,auth"}]}, "headerParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}]}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "14354e5f-bb8c-4fa7-852c-d82621fc03bd", "name": "Fetch Vulnerability Scan Results", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [96, 592], "parameters": {"url": "https://your-vulnerability-scanner.com/api/scan", "method": "POST", "options": {}, "sendBody": true, "sendHeaders": true, "bodyParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "scan_type", "value": "quick"}, {"name": "targets", "value": "internal_network"}]}, "headerParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE"}]}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "e6b1d20e-48e5-435f-bc96-621f95c6d1a5", "name": "Fetch Threat Intelligence Feed", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [96, 784], "parameters": {"url": "https://api.threatintel.com/v1/threats/recent", "options": {}, "sendHeaders": true, "headerParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "X-API-Key", "value": "YOUR_THREAT_INTEL_KEY"}]}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "52a555e8-19c0-4cc5-99a3-e780ac8cbc7e", "name": "Merge All Threat Data", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.merge", "position": [352, 592], "parameters": {}, "typeVersion": 3}, {"id": "2c8301ec-fa9a-4a4e-a7aa-f26357b26cef", "name": "Analyze & Detect Threats", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [608, 592], "parameters": {"jsCode": "// Threat Detection Logic\nconst items = $input.all();\nconst threats = [];\n\nfor (const item of items) {\n  const data = item.json;\n  \n  // Check for failed login attempts (Brute Force)\n  if (data.failed_logins && data.failed_logins > 10) {\n    threats.push({\n      severity: 'HIGH',\n      type: 'Brute Force Attack',\n      source: data.source_ip || 'Unknown',\n      description: `${data.failed_logins} failed login attempts detected`,\n      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n      action_required: 'Block IP and notify SOC'\n    });\n  }\n  \n  // Check for critical vulnerabilities\n  if (data.vulnerabilities) {\n    const criticalVulns = data.vulnerabilities.filter(v => v.severity === 'CRITICAL');\n    if (criticalVulns.length > 0) {\n      threats.push({\n        severity: 'CRITICAL',\n        type: 'Critical Vulnerability Detected',\n        affected_systems: data.hostname || 'Multiple systems',\n        description: `${criticalVulns.length} critical vulnerabilities found`,\n        timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n        action_required: 'Immediate patching required'\n      });\n    }\n  }\n  \n  // Check for suspicious traffic patterns\n  if (data.traffic_volume && data.traffic_volume > 10000) {\n    threats.push({\n      severity: 'MEDIUM',\n      type: 'Suspicious Traffic Pattern',\n      source: data.source_ip || 'Unknown',\n      description: `Abnormal traffic volume: ${data.traffic_volume} requests`,\n      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n      action_required: 'Investigate and monitor'\n    });\n  }\n  \n  // Check for malware signatures\n  if (data.malware_detected === true) {\n    threats.push({\n      severity: 'CRITICAL',\n      type: 'Malware Detection',\n      affected_systems: data.hostname || 'Unknown',\n      description: `Malware signature: ${data.malware_name || 'Unknown'}`,\n      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n      action_required: 'Isolate system immediately'\n    });\n  }\n  \n  // Check threat intelligence matches\n  if (data.ioc_match === true) {\n    threats.push({\n      severity: 'HIGH',\n      type: 'IOC Match',\n      indicator: data.indicator || 'Unknown',\n      description: `Known threat indicator detected: ${data.indicator_type}`,\n      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n      action_required: 'Block and investigate'\n    });\n  }\n}\n\nreturn threats.map(threat => ({ json: threat }));"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "e9494946-bdcd-41a9-b685-86cb6c5ddfd4", "name": "Check Threat Severity", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if", "position": [848, 592], "parameters": {"options": {}, "conditions": {"options": {"leftValue": "", "caseSensitive": true, "typeValidation": "strict"}, "combinator": "or", "conditions": [{"id": "condition-1", "operator": {"type": "string", "operation": "equals"}, "leftValue": "={{ $json.severity }}", "rightValue": "CRITICAL"}, {"id": "condition-2", "operator": {"type": "string", "operation": "equals"}, "leftValue": "={{ $json.severity }}", "rightValue": "HIGH"}]}}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "9c1414b8-f5cc-47da-a9de-909901adb984", "name": "Send Slack Alert - Critical", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack", "position": [1088, 464], "webhookId": "d6a0a10f-e8d2-4582-8575-c616319d80b6", "parameters": {"text": "=\ud83d\udea8 **SECURITY ALERT - {{ $json.severity }}**\n\n**Threat Type:** {{ $json.type }}\n**Source/System:** {{ $json.source || $json.affected_systems || $json.indicator }}\n**Description:** {{ $json.description }}\n**Time Detected:** {{ $json.timestamp }}\n**Action Required:** {{ $json.action_required }}\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Immediate response required!", "select": "channel", "channelId": {"__rl": true, "mode": "id", "value": "C12345678"}, "otherOptions": {}}, "credentials": {"slackApi": {"id": "5eb174b623cd4164", "name": "Dummy slackApi"}}, "typeVersion": 2.2}, {"id": "de4c0273-fa6e-4af0-9495-f78695e7e67f", "name": "Send Email Alert - Detailed", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.emailSend", "position": [1088, 672], "webhookId": "ce029cd9-3d2c-41d6-a482-33fb385b3356", "parameters": {"options": {}, "subject": "=\ud83d\udea8 {{ $json.severity }} Threat Detected: {{ $json.type }}", "toEmail": "user@example.com, user@example.com", "fromEmail": "user@example.com"}, "credentials": {"smtp": {"id": "aada66eae3214a41", "name": "Dummy smtp"}}, "typeVersion": 2.1}, {"id": "217d7550-3a07-4d86-b8aa-c7013ad4f165", "name": "Create PagerDuty Incident", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [1328, 464], "parameters": {"url": "https://api.pagerduty.com/incidents", "method": "POST", "options": {}, "jsonBody": "={\n  \"incident\": {\n    \"type\": \"incident\",\n    \"title\": \"{{ $json.severity }}: {{ $json.type }}\",\n    \"service\": {\n      \"id\": \"YOUR_SERVICE_ID\",\n      \"type\": \"service_reference\"\n    },\n    \"urgency\": \"high\",\n    \"body\": {\n      \"type\": \"incident_body\",\n      \"details\": \"{{ $json.description }}\\n\\nAction: {{ $json.action_required }}\"\n    }\n  }\n}", "sendBody": true, "sendHeaders": true, "specifyBody": "json", "headerParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "Authorization", "value": "Token token=YOUR_PAGERDUTY_KEY"}, {"name": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}, {"name": "Accept", "value": "application/vnd.pagerduty+json;version=2"}]}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "1cc4631b-7d8a-4231-ad8d-c8d70add7faa", "name": "Create Security Ticket", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [1328, 672], "parameters": {"url": "https://your-ticketing-system.com/api/tickets", "method": "POST", "options": {}, "jsonBody": "={\n  \"title\": \"{{ $json.severity }} Security Threat: {{ $json.type }}\",\n  \"description\": \"{{ $json.description }}\\n\\nDetected: {{ $json.timestamp }}\\nAction Required: {{ $json.action_required }}\",\n  \"priority\": \"{{ $json.severity === 'CRITICAL' ? 'P1' : 'P2' }}\",\n  \"category\": \"Security Incident\",\n  \"assigned_to\": \"SOC Team\"\n}", "sendBody": true, "sendHeaders": true, "specifyBody": "json", "headerParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE"}, {"name": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}]}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "cc06d7fd-96e9-4e91-b529-80eae70a9787", "name": "Log Medium/Low Threats", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [1088, 896], "parameters": {"url": "https://your-siem-system.com/api/events/log", "method": "POST", "options": {}, "jsonBody": "={\n  \"event_type\": \"security_threat\",\n  \"severity\": \"{{ $json.severity }}\",\n  \"threat_type\": \"{{ $json.type }}\",\n  \"description\": \"{{ $json.description }}\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"{{ $json.timestamp }}\",\n  \"source\": \"n8n_threat_detection\"\n}", "sendBody": true, "sendHeaders": true, "specifyBody": "json", "headerParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}]}}, "typeVersion": 4.2}, {"id": "2c5a881f-a51a-41bf-a00e-0f5ddc8beff5", "name": "Store in Database", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres", "position": [1344, 896], "parameters": {"query": "=INSERT INTO threat_log (severity, type, description, timestamp, action_required)\nVALUES (\n  '{{ $json.severity }}',\n  '{{ $json.type }}',\n  '{{ $json.description }}',\n  '{{ $json.timestamp }}',\n  '{{ $json.action_required }}'\n);", "options": {}, "operation": "executeQuery"}, "credentials": {"postgres": {"id": "ec83c6ee7ff2440d", "name": "Dummy postgres"}}, "typeVersion": 2.5}, {"id": "8199dd00-b0af-43c3-a5c6-346738debf86", "name": "Merge All Paths", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.merge", "position": [1568, 592], "parameters": {}, "typeVersion": 3}, {"id": "81cd1ef3-176a-4c56-b48a-429d24c9f659", "name": "Generate Summary Report", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [1808, 592], "parameters": {"jsCode": "// Generate Summary Report\nconst items = $input.all();\n\nconst summary = {\n  timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n  total_threats: items.length,\n  critical: items.filter(i => i.json.severity === 'CRITICAL').length,\n  high: items.filter(i => i.json.severity === 'HIGH').length,\n  medium: items.filter(i => i.json.severity === 'MEDIUM').length,\n  low: items.filter(i => i.json.severity === 'LOW').length,\n  threat_types: [...new Set(items.map(i => i.json.type))],\n  status: 'Workflow completed successfully'\n};\n\nreturn [{ json: summary }];"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "de5188a7-acc2-48e8-910a-61fdb4f25c7e", "name": "Send Summary to Monitoring Channel", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack", "position": [2048, 592], "webhookId": "c636bac1-5c75-4b12-98ca-4a9583026339", "parameters": {"text": "=\u2705 **Threat Detection Scan Complete**\n\n**Summary:**\n\u2022 Total Threats: {{ $json.total_threats }}\n\u2022 Critical: {{ $json.critical }}\n\u2022 High: {{ $json.high }}\n\u2022 Medium: {{ $json.medium }}\n\u2022 Low: {{ $json.low }}\n\n**Threat Types Detected:** {{ $json.threat_types.join(', ') }}\n\n**Scan Time:** {{ $json.timestamp }}", "select": "channel", "channelId": {"__rl": true, "mode": "id", "value": "C87654321"}, "otherOptions": {}}, "credentials": {"slackApi": {"id": "5eb174b623cd4164", "name": "Dummy slackApi"}}, "typeVersion": 2.2}, {"id": "webhook-automata-injected-1791111459348", "name": "Automata Webhook", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook", "position": [0, 0], "webhookId": "1dSFJgL340NlOBkh", "parameters": {"path": "1dSFJgL340NlOBkh", "options": {}, "httpMethod": "POST", "responseCode": 200, "responseMode": "onReceived"}, "typeVersion": 1.1}]
