 "required": false, "displayName": "hashtags", "defaultMatch": false, "canBeUsedToMatch": false}, {"id": "image_url", "type": "string", "display": true, "required": false, "displayName": "image_url", "defaultMatch": false, "canBeUsedToMatch": false}, {"id": "status", "type": "string", "display": true, "required": false, "displayName": "status", "defaultMatch": false, "canBeUsedToMatch": false}, {"id": "platforms", "type": "string", "display": true, "required": false, "displayName": "platforms", "defaultMatch": false, "canBeUsedToMatch": false}], "mappingMode": "defineBelow"}, "options": {}, "operation": "append", "sheetName": {"__rl": true, "mode": "name", "value": "linkedin"}, "documentId": {"__rl": true, "mode": "list", "value": "", "cachedResultName": "linkedin content"}}, "credentials": {"googleSheetsOAuth2Api": {"id": "cbc1b5f60f3e43a0", "name": "Dummy googleSheetsOAuth2Api"}}, "typeVersion": 4.7}, {"id": "187365b0-50ec-4e11-a2e0-2c8602f32194", "name": "Main sticky", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [-688, -624], "parameters": {"color": 3, "width": 640, "height": 1848, "content": "# Generate AI social posts and publish to multiple networks with Blotato\n# \ud83d\udce5  [Open full documentation on Notion](https://automatisation.notion.site/Course-Generate-AI-social-posts-and-publish-to-multiple-networks-with-Blotato-39a3d6550fd981e29df3f2a5cd8cc5c6)\n\n# \ud83d\udce5  [Copy my Google Sheets](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1UD41eCVTGJYZxqVUElnD8OJZkfB541IQ0LyPUtdqOvQ/copy)\n\n\n## How it works\nOn a schedule, GPT picks a fresh content topic in your niche, writes a ready-to-post caption in your voice, and generates a matching image with DALL\u00b7E. You get a Telegram message with the post + image and two buttons (Publish / Skip). Only after you approve, the post is published to LinkedIn, X, Instagram, Facebook and Threads via [Blotato](https://blotato.com/?ref=firas). Every run is logged to Google Sheets. The AI proposes, you approve before anything goes live.\n\n## Setup\n1. Open the **Configuration** node: set your language, niche, audience, tone, image style and **telegram_chat_id** (ask @get_id_bot on Telegram for your ID).\n2. Select your **OpenAi account** credential on the two model nodes and on **Generate image**.\n3. Select your **Telegram account** credential on **Approve on Telegram**.\n4. On each **Publish to \u2026** node, select your **Blotato account** credential and pick the matching social account in the dropdown.\n5. On both Google Sheets nodes, select your **Google Sheets account**, then pick the log spreadsheet and the `linkedin` tab.\n\n## Requirements\n- n8n **self-hosted** (or Cloud with Verified Community Nodes) \u2014 this template uses the [Blotato](https://blotato.com/?ref=firas) community node.\n- An OpenAI API key, a [Blotato](https://blotato.com/?ref=firas) account with your networks connected, a Telegram bot, and a Google Sheet.\n- DALL\u00b7E 3 image cost \u2248 $0.04 per image; GPT text cost is a few cents per run.\n\n## Customization\n- Change the schedule (default: every 24h) on **Run on schedule**.\n- Add or remove networks by duplicating / deleting a **Publish to \u2026** node (set its `platform`).\n- Tune the topic and writing prompts in **Generate content topic** and **Write post**.\n- Note: X (Twitter) has a 280-character limit \u2014 keep captions short or let Blotato handle threading.\n\n---\nNeed help customizing?\nContact me for consulting and support : [Linkedin](https://www.linkedin.com/in/doctor-firass/)\n\n# MY NEW YOUTUBE CHANNEL\n\ud83d\udc49 [Subscribe to my new YouTube channel](https://www.youtube.com/@DrFiras_AI). Here I'll share videos and Shorts with practical tutorials and FREE templates for n8n.\n\n[![The AI Doctor](https://www.dr-firas.com/the-ai-doctor.png)](https://www.youtube.com/@DrFiras_AI)"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "c3cf9750-dbaf-47af-9981-fe64e363eadb", "name": "Sticky 1", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [368, -176], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 520, "height": 520, "content": "## 1. Configure & generate\nSet every adjustable variable in **Configuration** (language, niche, audience, models, telegram_chat_id). GPT then picks a topic and writes the post + image prompt + hashtags."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "5ad75215-433e-409e-891c-af49e38c1ef8", "name": "Sticky 2", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [880, -176], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 420, "height": 520, "content": "## 2. Create the visual\nDALL\u00b7E generates a matching image and returns its URL for the post."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "4fece39c-df80-4d4c-9719-57120647a005", "name": "Sticky 3", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1328, -176], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 420, "height": 520, "content": "## 3. Review & approve\nA Telegram message shows the post + image with Publish / Skip buttons. Nothing is posted without your approval."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "4381afe1-fe52-4b8f-a27f-c0dab493f69e", "name": "Sticky 4", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1760, -304], "parameters": {"color": 7, "width": 1240, "height": 400, "content": "## 4. Publish & log\nOn approval, the post goes to LinkedIn, X, Instagram, Facebook and Threads via Blotato, then the run is logged to Google Sheets (Skipped runs are logged too)."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "webhook-automata-injected-1791111459382", "name": "Automata Webhook", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook", "position": [0, 0], "webhookId": "sIc6gsuo1dB3WOkA", "parameters": {"path": "sIc6gsuo1dB3WOkA", "options": {}, "httpMethod": "POST", "responseCode": 200, "responseMode": "onReceived"}, "typeVersion": 1.1}]
ZjppPToVEhX437yL|[{"id": "0c2cd139-a7b1-4a3f-863e-37b2615b281c", "name": "Sticky Note - Overview", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [1072, -2080], "parameters": {"width": 1080, "height": 996, "content": "## Secrets & API Key Exposure Monitor\n\nScans recent Git activity and CI/CD logs for accidentally committed credentials, checks whether flagged secrets are STILL LIVE against their issuing provider, and runs a genuine remediation loop: alert -> human confirms they've rotated it -> a timed grace period -> automatic re-verification -> either close the case or escalate again if the key is somehow still active.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Import this workflow into n8n\n2. Add credentials: your Git host API (repo node), your CI/CD platform API (CI logs node), a generic auth for the verification node (it's reused for GitHub/Stripe-style bearer-token checks), and WhatsApp Business Cloud API credentials on every WhatsApp node\n3. Edit Set - Config: repoOwner/repoName/baseBranch, ciApiUrl, whatsappBusinessPhoneId, whatsappRecipientPhone\n4. Point Wait - For Remediation Confirmation's resume webhook at your on-call tool's 'mark rotated' action\n5. Activate the workflow, or use the Manual Trigger to test end to end\n\n### Requirements\n- Git hosting API access (commits/diffs)\n- CI/CD platform API access (build logs)\n- WhatsApp Business Cloud API credentials\n\n### A note on the raw secret value\nThe actual matched string is kept ONLY in an internal field used to test validity against the issuing provider — every outward-facing message (WhatsApp text, the report payload) uses the masked value exclusively. Turn off execution-data logging or use n8n's data-pruning settings for this workflow, since even internal fields are still part of execution history.\n\n### How to customize\n- Add more regex patterns (Azure, Twilio, SendGrid, npm tokens, etc.) to the first code node\n- Wire the 'cloud' verification branch to a properly SigV4-signed AWS call (STS GetCallerIdentity) instead of the illustrative placeholder\n- Adjust the severity score weights or the grace-period duration in Wait - For Re-Verification Grace Period"}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "f361b523-cc20-4390-9022-0c055ea7a463", "name": "Sticky Note - Scan Sources & Detection", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [2336, -2112], "parameters": {"color": 4, "width": 940, "height": 900, "content": "## 1. Trigger, Data Sources & Detection\n\nSet - Config centralizes every API URL and the WhatsApp sender details.\n\nHTTP Request - Fetch Recent Repository Commits/Diffs and HTTP Request - Fetch CI/CD Pipeline Logs are the first two of the workflow's three API calls, pulling raw text to scan.\n\nJS - Scan Content for Secret Patterns & Compute Entropy Scores is the first code node: ~10 named-provider regexes plus a Shannon-entropy filter on generic key=value assignments, deduped and masked, emitted as one item per finding so everything downstream (verification, severity routing) runs per-secret."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "b8fe32df-c99d-4ef9-a6f8-bf68e5f7e583", "name": "Sticky Note - Verification Routing", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [3312, -2160], "parameters": {"color": 3, "width": 1124, "height": 1204, "content": "## 2. Switch-Routed Verification\n\nSwitch - Secret Type Category is the first switch: cloud/VCS/payment findings each get routed through a small Set node that configures a different target URL and auth header, then all three converge on the SAME HTTP Request - Verify Credential Validity call (the workflow's third API node) — one shared verification node, dynamically configured per finding. Generic high-entropy matches can't be verified against a specific provider, so they skip straight to risk classification instead.\n\nThis same verification node is reused later for the post-remediation re-check — IF - Is Reverification Pass tells the two passes apart and routes each to the right next step."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "c273d8ed-a493-43a3-ab56-2b5e1bb15dfe", "name": "Sticky Note - Severity Routing & Remediation Loop", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "position": [4480, -2176], "parameters": {"color": 5, "width": 1816, "height": 1284, "content": "## 3. Risk Scoring, Severity Switch & Remediation Loop\n\nJS - Classify Risk & Build Remediation Plan is the second code node: scores severity from secret type, source (repo vs. CI), live/revoked status, and builds a per-type remediation checklist.\n\nSwitch - Severity Routing is the second switch: critical/high goes into the full loop, medium gets a single WhatsApp notice, low gets logged only.\n\nThe loop: WhatsApp - Send Urgent Alert -> Wait - For Remediation Confirmation (webhook resume) -> IF - Remediation Confirmed (unconfirmed loops back to the same Wait after a reminder) -> Wait - For Re-Verification Grace Period (a genuine TIME-based wait, not webhook resume) -> Set - Prepare Reverification -> back through the shared verification call -> IF - Still Valid After Remediation decides between escalating again or closing the case as confirmed-revoked."}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "f769e224-4394-4180-8036-045768263dde", "name": "Schedule Trigger - Every 6 Hours", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger", "position": [2432, -1664], "parameters": {"rule": {"interval": [{"field": "cronExpression", "expression": "0 */6 * * *"}]}}, "typeVersion": 1.2}, {"id": "32f7603a-be7f-4b98-aad5-a371c63711bd", "name": "Manual Trigger - Test Run", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger", "position": [2432, -1472], "parameters": {}, "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "8afb5e19-ada2-4d30-b330-d3186ea4e661", "name": "Set - Config", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set", "position": [2656, -1584], "parameters": {"options": {}, "assignments": {"assignments": [{"name": "repoOwner", "type": "string", "value": "your-org"}, {"name": "repoName", "type": "string", "value": "your-repo"}, {"name": "baseBranch", "type": "string", "value": "main"}, {"name": "ciApiUrl", "type": "string", "value": "https://api.yourci.com/v1/projects/your-project/logs"}, {"name": "whatsappBusinessPhoneId", "type": "string", "value": "your-whatsapp-phone-number-id"}, {"name": "whatsappRecipientPhone", "type": "string", "value": "+1234567890"}]}}, "typeVersion": 3.4}, {"id": "b8f7c739-f5fd-4d32-8a28-a7c2267a2785", "name": "HTTP Request - Fetch Recent Repository Commits/Diffs", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [2880, -1584], "parameters": {"url": "=https://api.github.com/repos/{{ $json.repoOwner }}/{{ $json.repoName }}/commits", "options": {}, "sendQuery": true, "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType", "queryParameters": {"parameters": [{"name": "sha", "value": "={{ $json.baseBranch }}"}, {"name": "per_page", "value": "20"}]}, "nodeCredentialType": "githubApi"}, "typeVersion": 4.2, "continueOnFail": true}, {"id": "11b8a388-59e7-4cd2-b4cb-799035b0952c", "name": "HTTP Request - Fetch CI/CD Pipeline Logs", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", "position": [3104, -1584], "parameters": {"url": "={{ $('Set - Config').item.json.ciApiUrl }}", "options": {}, "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType", "nodeCredentialType": "httpHeaderAuth"}, "typeVersion": 4.2, "continueOnFail": true}, {"id": "f3703b87-edb1-4cc8-8c2e-828185e379ac", "name": "JS - Scan Content for Secret Patterns & Compute Entropy Scores", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "position": [3328, -1584], "parameters": {"jsCode": "// Advanced detection: named-provider regexes + Shannon-entropy filtering on\n// generic key=value assignments, deduped and masked, one item per finding.\nconst cfg = $('Set - Config').first().json;\nconst repoData = $('HTTP Request - Fetch Recent Repository Commits/Diffs').first().json;\nconst ciData = $('HTTP Request - Fetch CI/CD Pipeline Logs').first().json;\n\nconst repoContent = (repoData.files || repoData || []).map ? (repoData.files || []).map(f => ({ source: 'repo', location: f.filename || f.path || 'unknown', text: f.patch || f.content || '' })) : [];\nconst ciContent = (ciData.logs || []).map((l, i) => ({ source: 'ci', location: 'log-line-' + i, text: String(l) }));\nconst sources = [...repoContent, ...ciContent];\n\nconst PATTERNS = [\n  { type: 'AWS Access Key', category: 'cloud', re: /AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}/g },\n  { type: 'AWS Secret Key', category: 'cloud', re: /[A-Za-z0-9\\/+]{40}/g },\n  { type: 'GitHub Personal Access Token', category: 'vcs', re: /gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{36,255}/g },\n  { type: 'GitLab Token', category: 'vcs', re: /glpat-[A-Za-z0-9\\-_]{20}/g },\n  { type: 'Slack Token', category: 'vcs', re: /xox[baprs]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,72}/g },\n  { type: 'Stripe Live Key', category: 'payment', re: /sk_live_[0-9a-zA-Z]{24,}/g },\n  { type: 'Stripe Restricted Key', category: 'payment', re: /rk_live_[0-9a-zA-Z]{24,}/g },\n  { type: 'Google API Key', category: 'cloud', re: /AIza[0-9A-Za-z\\-_]{35}/g },\n  { type: 'Private Key Block', category: 'cloud', re: /-----BEGIN (RSA |EC |)PRIVATE KEY-----/g },\n  { type: 'Generic Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE', category: 'generic', re: /Bearer\\s+[A-Za-z0-9\\-\\._~\\+\\/]{20,}/g }\n];\n\nfunction shannonEntropy(str) {\n  const freq = {};\n  for (const ch of str) freq[ch] = (freq[ch] || 0) + 1;\n  let entropy = 0;\n  const len = str.length;\n  for (const ch in freq) {\n    const p = freq[ch] / len;\n    entropy -= p * Math.log2(p);\n  }\n  return entropy;\n}\n\nfunction maskValue(value) {\n  if (value.length <= 8) return '***';\n  return value.slice(0, 4) + '...' + value.slice(-4);\n}\n\nconst findingsMap = new Map();\n\nfor (const src of sources) {\n  for (const pattern of PATTERNS) {\n    const matches = src.text.match(pattern.re) || [];\n    for (const match of matches) {\n      const entropy = shannonEntropy(match);\n      if (pattern.category === 'generic' && entropy < 3.5) continue;\n      const masked = maskValue(match);\n      const key = pattern.type + ':' + masked;\n      if (findingsMap.has(key)) continue;\n      findingsMap.set(key, {\n        secretType: pattern.type,\n        category: pattern.category,\n        source: src.source,\n        location: src.location,\n        maskedValue: masked,\n        rawValueForVerificationOnly: match,\n        entropyScore: Math.round(entropy * 100) / 100,\n        confidencePercent: pattern.category === 'generic' ? Math.min(90, Math.round(entropy * 20)) : 95\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Generic .env-style KEY=value assignments not caught by a named pattern\n  const kvMatches = src.text.match(/[A-Z0-9_]{4,}\\s*[:=]\\s*['\"]?([A-Za-z0-9\\/+_\\-]{20,})['\"]?/g) || [];\n  for (const kv of kvMatches) {\n    const valueMatch = kv.match(/['\"]?([A-Za-z0-9\\/+_\\-]{20,})['\"]?$/);\n    if (!valueMatch) continue;\n    const value = valueMatch[1];\n    const entropy = shannonEntropy(value);\n    if (entropy < 4.0) continue;\n    const masked = maskValue(value);\n    const key = 'Generic High-Entropy String:' + masked;\n    if (findingsMap.has(key)) continue;\n    findingsMap.set(key, {\n      secretType: 'Generic High-Entropy String',\n      category: 'generic',\n      source: src.source,\n      location: src.location,\n      maskedValue: masked,\n      rawValueForVerificationOnly: value,\n      entropyScore: Math.round(entropy * 100) / 100,\n      confidencePercent: Math.min(85, Math.round(entropy * 18))\n    });\n  }\n}\n\nconst findings = [...findingsMap.values()];\n\nif (findings.length === 0) {\n  return [{ json: { ...cfg, noFindings: true } }];\n}\n\nreturn findings.map(f => ({ json: { ...cfg, ...f, noFindings: false } }));"}, "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "8b78f321-2c07-4aa7-a031-0e7b4d1dca29", "name": "Switch - Secret Type Category", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.switch", "position": [3552, -1584], "parameters": {"rules": {"values": [{"conditions": {"options": {"version": 1, "leftValue": "", "caseSensitive": true, "typeValidation": "strict"}, "combinator": "and", "conditions": [{"operator": {"type": "string", "operation": "equals"}, "leftValue": "={{ $json.category }}", "rightValue": "cloud"}]}}, {"conditions": {"options": {"version": 1, "leftValue": "", "caseSensitive": true, "typeValidation": "strict"}, "combinator": "and", "conditions": [{"operator": {"type": "string", "operation": "equals"}, "leftValue": "={{ $json.category }}", "rightValue": "vcs"}]}}, {"conditions": {"options": {"version": 1, "leftValue": "", "caseSensitive": true, "typeValidation": "strict"}, "combinator": "and", "conditions": [{"operator": {"type": "string", "operation": "equals"}, "leftValue": "={{ $json.category }}", "rightValue": "payment"}]}}]}, "options": {"fallbackOutput": "extra"}}, "typeVersion": 3.2}, {"id": "9eef6492-29fc-4549-8413-52cc4d8fede3", "name": "Set - Cloud Verification Params", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set", "position": [3792, -1760], "parameters": {"options": {}, "assignments": {"assignments": [{"name": "verificationPass", "type": "string", "value": "initial"}, {"name": "verificationApiUrl", "type": "string", "value": "https://sts.amazonaws.com/?Action=GetCallerIdentity&Version=2011-06-15"}, {"name": "verificationAuthHeader", "type": "string", "value": ""}, {"name": "verificationNote", "type": "string", "value": "AWS requires SigV4-signed requests — wire a proper AWS credential node here for production; this is a placeholder endpoint."}]}}, "typeVersion": 3.4}, {"id": "cffafb4c-a4a8-4a61-8d6a-f2cb5482fd6b", "name": "Set - VCS Verification Params", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set", "position": [3792, -1584], "parameters": {"options": {}, "assignments": {"assignments": [{"name": "verificationPass", "type": "string", "value": "initial"}, {"name": "verificationApiUrl", "type": "string", "value": "https://api.github.com/user"}, {"name": "verificationAuthHeader", "type": "string", "value": "={{ 'Bearer ' + $json.rawValueForVerificationOnly }}"}]}}, "typeVersion": 3.4}, {"id": "3e327ae5-1d28-4447-86c6-35837fd5acc7", "name": "Set - Payment Verification Params", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set", "position": [3792, -1408], "parameters": {"options": {}, "assignments": {"assignments": [{"name": "verification